---
title: Hardware fit, GGUF metadata, and conversations
date: '2026-06-16'
tags:
  - added
summary: Source added hardware-fit estimates, GGUF metadata reading, GPU-layer settings, and conversation archive, rename, and delete controls. Native runtime verification remains open.
---
This source milestone added ways to estimate model fit and inspect GGUF metadata
before deciding what to run. GPU-layer settings, conversation archive, rename,
delete, and system-prompt persistence were also added to the desktop UI. These
paths have not completed a native end-to-end test in this review; hardware-fit
estimates are not a guarantee that a model will load or run well.

The earlier paired images showed an old marketing landing, not the native app.
They visibly promised a working waitlist, zero network egress, and suitability
for regulated work. We withdrew them because the current source makes outbound
model-download requests and establishes no compliance certification. A real
paired capture of the verified desktop workflow is still needed.
